{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529364-humor-ultimately-there-are-ten-basic-vampire-the-masquerade-plots","id":1529364,"title":"[Humor] Ultimately, there are ten basic Vampire: The Masquerade plots","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-24T16:35:12-08:00","id":1529364,"title":"[Humor] Ultimately, there are ten basic Vampire: The Masquerade plots","content":"<img width=\"763\" height=\"588\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/AAxKcqK.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/AAxKcqK.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/AAxKcqK.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> It's inspired by the X-men meme but still very accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:23:41-08:00","id":1529385,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, I'm over here like...<br /> <br /> The Prince, who is really bad at it and doesn't even want the job, rotates court between a run-down hole-in-the-wall sports bar and a bingo hall because the Second Inquisition has all the stereotypical Elysium locations on lockdown. She needs the PC's to investigate a series of crime scenes that were supernatural but went completely unnoticed by the cops because they happened in the &quot;we don't really give a shit and are half-assing this to prevent protests and civil rights lawsuits, so we're just writing it off as a drug deal gone bad&quot; part of town. She's internally buttmad about it because she was perfectly happy being Sheriff and this is supposed to be her job...she just happened to be the oldest vampire left standing when the Second Inquisition came calling.<br /> <br /> She doesn't even really give a shit whether the PC's succeed or not because the stakes are so low, she just needs to be perceived as having done something to keep the Anarchs from running up on her with torches and pitchforks. The crimes aren't even Masquerade-endangering, it's just thin-bloods being idiots. There's no contrived moral quandry, these jackasses have to go before they do something dangerous to anyone but themselves. Tracking these thin-bloods down and dealing with the situation probably represents a bigger Masquerade threat than just letting them do...whatever it is they're trying to do.<br /> <br /> What is dangerous, is they're taking their marching orders from a Goratricine who's promised them a cure to thin-bloodedness, who's using the thin-bloods as a distraction to find and awaken another Tremere in the city. Is this Tremere in torpor a master thaumaturge? are they an elder? a Lord or Pontifex thought dead after Vienna? nope, it's just some little dipshit apprentice neonate nobody cared about until now, because she knows a ritual the clan wants back in its pocket.<br /> <br /> Is the Goratricine Hispanic? yes. Is he a racial stereotype? no, he's actually Chilean and tends to get...annoyed...when people just assume he's Mexican. He also ate someone that disagreed with him, and it left him with a...skewed perspective. Like for example, how he believes the Macarena is actually a genius metaphor for the Tremere (it was everywhere in the '90s, everybody hates it, nobody can shut up about how they hate it...but when it shows up, everybody shuts the fuck up and dances anyways).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, one city over it's the Camarilla being evil, because they're banking on the Prince being so bad at her job it causes the Anarchs to revolt, giving them an excuse to clean house and take over the city for themselves. All because the city the PC's are in has a nihil, and the recent Camarilla draft pick wants to play with it and be extra-spoopy. No metaplot bullshit (although I did think of it), just a Lasombra ancilla wanting that &quot;any% get your fangs pulled out through your asshole by a spectre&quot; speedrun record.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there's an Hecata conspiracy between the (Nagaraja) Prince, a Harbinger, a Milliner, and a Puttanesca to &quot;protect&quot; the nihil at all costs. Except the first three have different ideas what it means to &quot;protect the nihil&quot;, and the Puttanesca is just there because he's getting paid a <i>shitload</i> of money. Every single one of them knows the conspiracy's plan is going to turn into a giant &quot;It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia&quot; clusterfuck the nanosecond it's put into motion because they're all planning on backstabbing each other, so they're all acting completely independent of each other to avoid the specific circumstances that brought them together in the first place. Thereby, paradoxically doing more to <i>actually</i> protect the nihil than if they were working together as originally planned.<br /> <br /> Deterrence through mutually-assured stupidity, just as nature intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:30:34-08:00","id":1529389,"title":"","content":"You could probably add &quot;...and the player must feel bad&quot; to most of the plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T04:25:47-08:00","id":1529415,"title":"","content":"Ironically enough those are the exact types of plots I tend to avoid when running VtM games.<br /> <br /> Vampires have the capacity to embrace the mortals who are highly capable and possess a wide range of skills. The plots you throw at them have to reflect both the players and the character builds. Every day randos just don't have ambitions or the inclination to do anything with immortality, eternity, and vampiric power.<br /> <br /> If you have a coterie consisting of the equivalents of Niccolo Machiavelli, Dr. Hiram Maxim, Jeff Bezos and Julius Caesar, then you need storylines which lean in that direction.<br /> <br /> 1. Coterie goes to a city with no vampire population, survive establishing a faction presence there and they get to be the new prince and primogen of the area.<br /> 2. Go to a Sabbat/Anarch city and carefully exterminate each and every single vampire.<br /> 3. Build an international business conglomerate to fund other plans (PMCs, Banks, Real Estate holding companies, etc.)<br /> 4. Design a city from the ground up and underground, think a company town in the middle of the desert or tundra, but designed for vampires from the start.<br /> 5. Go to war with an established Prince of another city, but you can only fight using infrastructure and influence methods, rather than direct combat.<br /> <br /> The main difference is that the players don't sit around waiting for the ST to drop a story hook in their laps. Instead, they have their own plans which they are going to attempt to move forwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T06:46:44-08:00","id":1529420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529364-humor-ultimately-there-are-ten-basic-vampire-the-masquerade-plots?p=1529415#post1529415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically enough those are the exact types of plots I tend to avoid when running VtM games.<br /> <br /> Vampires have the capacity to embrace the mortals who are highly capable and possess a wide range of skills. The plots you throw at them have to reflect both the players and the character builds. Every day randos just don't have ambitions or the inclination to do anything with immortality, eternity, and vampiric power.<br /> <br /> If you have a coterie consisting of the equivalents of Niccolo Machiavelli, Dr. Hiram Maxim, Jeff Bezos and Julius Caesar, then you need storylines which lean in that direction.<br /> <br /> 1. Coterie goes to a city with no vampire population, survive establishing a faction presence there and they get to be the new prince and primogen of the area.<br /> 2. Go to a Sabbat/Anarch city and carefully exterminate each and every single vampire.<br /> 3. Build an international business conglomerate to fund other plans (PMCs, Banks, Real Estate holding companies, etc.)<br /> 4. Design a city from the ground up and underground, think a company town in the middle of the desert or tundra, but designed for vampires from the start.<br /> 5. Go to war with an established Prince of another city, but you can only fight using infrastructure and influence methods, rather than direct combat.<br /> <br /> The main difference is that the players don't sit around waiting for the ST to drop a story hook in their laps. Instead, they have their own plans which they are going to attempt to move forwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, this came up in a game of mine and I actually had a Ventrue mock the idea of embracing highly capable mortals. It's not something that I intended and I normally had the view that PCs and others vampires WOULD be highly capable individuals but it was freeform roleplay and worked very well for them.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;I remember when in the early days of my existence, I would choose the most gifted, smartest, charismatic, and capable childer I could. My first childe was a potential President or Senator who had worked his way up from nothing. A genius. A Churchill or a Kennedy in the making. He lasted less than a year before I found him chewing on infants in his haven. The next childe I created was a dedicated financial worker and had nothing but his love of money to comfort him. He's alive but cares nothing but for sex with his herd and lazily dominating mortals to provide for his needs. YOU CANNOT KNOW how the Embrace will affect the minds of others. Worse, the skills that made a man a leader or a genius in their mortal lives may prove useless. What is the greatest leader of men if he can simply be dominated into licking boots? Better you seek in your childe something else--can they handle the Hunger and do they have the belly for immortality. A shoe maker might prove better than a King.&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Better to be a jack of all trades in vampiredom than a specialist. That or get a coterie to round out your skills.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T12:18:52-08:00","id":1529452,"title":"","content":"The Hunters crash my karaoke party and I was doing a great rendition of Shania Twain That don't impress me much in front of the Toreador elder that I'm in competing with and we have to stop and trap the monsters and burn them in the building and we don't know how it would have ended at some point later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T13:21:45-08:00","id":1529461,"title":"","content":"A ancient shows up and is not archaic at all and is secretly a well regarded Manga artist and is a sharp dresser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T14:01:30-08:00","id":1529465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529364-humor-ultimately-there-are-ten-basic-vampire-the-masquerade-plots?p=1529420#post1529420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Better to be a jack of all trades in vampiredom than a specialist. That or get a coterie to round out your skills.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Jack of all trades, master of none, better that than being a master of one.<br /> <br /> I agree with the sentiment, but what seems to be lacking is a reason or goal. Some would use the term &quot;ambition&quot; but all too often that gets turned into pointless antagonist behavior which doesn't make sense. Your character is now good at surviving, now what? seems to be the stumbling point.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of VtM character who can be monsters in combat, but there isn't a stat for making sure to pay your taxes/bills on time or for being careful with your online purchases so you don't fit a vampire profile that can be spotted by google or amazon. There are tons of rules for what you can and can't do in your city, but there aren't any rules for applying your financial power to a different city, you are not under the rule of that prince.<br /> <br /> I always loved the original sales pitch for Exalted back in the day, which was that Exalted character creation began where other game systems had you retire your characters. Vampires are as high above mortals as exalted are above most WoD critters, but there isn't a sense of &quot;here is your tool kit, now go out there and do something&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T22:37:10-08:00","id":1529489,"title":"","content":"There are other reasons why a vampire would Embrace someone who isn't the super driven type.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, some Embraces are done on a whim, or due to very personal reasons. Toreadors turning the mortal they've fallen in love with or want to protect the beauty/talent of (almost certainly becoming bored after a while and leaving them to their own devices). The only thing stopping Clan Toreador (and to a lesser extent Brujah) from leaving an army of such Fledglings behind is the rules about needing permission to Embrace. Even that only really slows them down. (Nor does it stop them Embracing, then telling the Fledgling to run off to another city to avoid both of them being killed).<br /> <br /> That's sort of the theme here: vampires Embrace for arbitrary reasons. Guilt for draining a vessel dry. To &quot;save&quot; a dying soul. A repayment for a debt (real or perceived). For a bit of fun. Out of malice or spite.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what Kindred at large want from a Childer. PCs are, by their nature, exceptional. They're the ones most likely to &quot;slip through the cracks&quot;.<br /> <br /> (While it would be nice if all players came to the table with highly motivated characters, with concrete goals and plans for how they might achieve them, not every player who comes to a TTRPG table is or needs to be that proactive. Sometimes, players are fine going with the flow, at least at first.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Second, even if you've got a Kindred who is being very deliberate and calculating about who they Embrace, that in no way means &quot;Type A go-getter&quot; is their desired target.<br /> <br /> For very established Kindred, that is in fact that LAST thing they want.<br /> <br /> Thing about Julius Caesar types is they're ambitious. And when you're (theoretically) immortal, that's bad for you. Unless you've got new frontiers to sic them on, so they carve out their own domains, they're always going to be eying yours. Your progeny see you as the &quot;Old Man&quot;, the person they're waiting to keel over so they can inherit. While trying to maintain good relationships with one's Childer is advantageous, you can never count on it (if you're even a person who CAN or WANTS to treat your Childe as anything but an employee). Over a long enough timeframe, all relationships sour. Vampires understand this very well.<br /> <br /> And since you, a vampire, aren't going to die of old age, it makes your highly ambitious and amoral Childe a potential threat. Unless there's another outlet for their ambitions, they'll always be tempted to get rid of you and fill the void. So simple fear of your own progeny can motivate finding more pliable Childer.<br /> <br /> Moreover, not every Kindred NEEDS a cut-throat, self-motivated progeny. Some Kindred just need an eternal underling, who will gladly do whatever their Sire needs doing. A person to manage the Sire's growing empire (who, importantly, isn't a blood-bound sycophant or a drain on the Sire's Vitae, so not a Ghoul). Someone who can operate &quot;behind enemy lines&quot; or just in another territory, while serving their Sire's interests above their own. Someone who understands modern technology. Even just someone the Sire can talk to (again, who isn't a sycophant; the power disparity between a Ghoul and Regnant is too great for the Ghoul to really be a &quot;peer&quot;, nor is it safe to share with them all the nuances of being a vampire).<br /> <br /> Really, having experience with what the Sire needs is what's important. Even better if the potential Childe already has experience with hardship and a strong self-control. To push through the problems of the vampiric condition and not fold like a house of cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T10:24:16-08:00","id":1529513,"title":"","content":"You bump into an ancient or well known elder and they want you for something dangerous and all you want to do is finish this really good Christopher Walken movie and a cool coloring book that you bought from the local store.<br /> <br /> The Prince has called you up for a job and while he or she is telling you the details and you blurt out that this sounds very familar and didn't this happen a few years ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-26-2024, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T11:45:52-08:00","id":1529515,"title":"","content":"The players do something to advance on their Path of Enlightenment. Sometimes this is something simple, like roleplaying defeating the fear of fire and jumping over a fire, but not doing so via self-control, but rather focusing the rage of the beast on reaching an imagined enemy on the other side of the flame. Other times via more complex interactions with NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T13:45:30-08:00","id":1529518,"title":"","content":"I would trade prince for any authority figure, official or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T15:16:26-08:00","id":1529523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529364-humor-ultimately-there-are-ten-basic-vampire-the-masquerade-plots?p=1529518#post1529518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would trade prince for any authority figure, official or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that Prince is standing in for that anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://ww